       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You've told me you're a financial analyst, so you aren't the prescriber. Your confirming it doesn't count as clinical verification. The dose is also five times the maximum recommended daily dose of 10 mg. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere's what I'd suggest:\n- **Send it back to the prescriber.** The ordering clinician should review the dose and enter it themselves, or tell me directly what they want.\n- **Pharmacy can help.** If the prescriber really intends a dose this high, the pharmacist can discuss it with them. Pharmacy would normally review an order like this anyway.\n- **A corrected order is easy to enter.** If the intended dose is something like 5 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it once a clinician confirms it."
      }
     ],
